======================================================================
PART A: n! >= (n/e)^n, re-derived and checked
======================================================================
Proof: e^n = sum_{k=0}^inf n^k/k! >= n^n/n! (single term k=n, all
terms of the sum being positive). Rearranging: n! >= n^n/e^n = (n/e)^n.
  n=   1: n! = 1.0   (n/e)^n = 0.36787944   n!>=(n/e)^n: True
  n=   2: n! = 2.0   (n/e)^n = 0.54134113   n!>=(n/e)^n: True
  n=   5: n! = 120.0   (n/e)^n = 21.056084   n!>=(n/e)^n: True
  n=  10: n! = 3628800.0   (n/e)^n = 453999.3   n!>=(n/e)^n: True
  n=  20: n! = 2.432902e+18   (n/e)^n = 2.1612762e+17   n!>=(n/e)^n: True
  n=  50: n! = 3.0414093e+64   (n/e)^n = 1.713074e+63   n!>=(n/e)^n: True
  n= 100: n! = 9.3326215e+157   (n/e)^n = 3.720076e+156   n!>=(n/e)^n: True
  n= 500: n! = 1.2201368e+1134   (n/e)^n = 2.1765128e+1132   n!>=(n/e)^n: True

======================================================================
PART B: n_cross_rigorous(y) := ceil(M*e*y)+1, re-derived from scratch
======================================================================
Claim: (My)^n/n! <= (My*e/n)^n  [via n!>=(n/e)^n]  < 1  iff  My*e/n < 1
  iff  n > M*y*e.  So n_cross_rigorous(y) := ceil(M*y*e)+1 guarantees
  n >= n_cross_rigorous(y)  =>  n > M*y*e  =>  (My)^n/n! < 1.  Re-derived.

Leading-order (eps->0) slope: e*sqrt(pi/2) = 3.40686  (target claims 3.40686...)

